# tools/cr/crypto_eip712_witness.rish — the Ethereum EIP-712 typed-structured-data hashing scheme, authored in pure Rye as a composition over three
# already-GREEN rungs: the Keccak-256 (crypto/keccak256.rye), the ECDSA public-key recovery (crypto/secp256k1_ecrecover.rye), and the address
# derivation (crypto/eth_address.rye). EIP-712 is the digest a wallet shows a human before it signs "typed data" — every EIP-2612 token permit,
# every DeFi order (0x, Seaport, Permit2), every gasless meta-transaction, and every typed Sign-in-with-Ethereum runs through this exact
# construction. Where EIP-191 personal_sign frames a flat string, EIP-712 hashes a TREE of typed fields against a domain separator, so a signature
# for one contract on one chain can never be replayed against another (crypto · Season G · Cryptography).
#
# Season: crypto — Season G (the Six-Season double-seat). This rung authors NO new cryptography: every hash is the GREEN Keccak-256, every recovery
# the GREEN ecrecover, every address the GREEN eth_address — it contributes only the EIP-712 encoding (type hash, struct hash, domain separator, and
# the 0x1901 digest framing) over stones already proven on metal beneath it, widening the Kumara-login / Dimeroll-receipt door from flat messages to
# typed structured data. Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-175524_rye-first-crypto-parity-and-the-decision-wave.md (Season G · the crypto
# parity wave). Clean-room: EIP-712 is Ethereum's own public standard; the encoding is ours, standing on our own parity-GREEN rungs, never a copied
# line (.claude/rules/gratitude-licenses.md).
#
# Parity is proven at selftest three ways runnable now: (1) a PUBLISHED known-answer bound to the world — the EIP-712 spec's own canonical Ether
# Mail example (Cow -> Bob), assembled from our building blocks, is recovered by the spec's own published 65-byte signature to exactly Cow's
# published wallet 0xCD2a...D826 (a one-bit encoding error would break the recovery); (2) an INDEPENDENT construction — our digest equals a second
# built entirely from Zig's std.crypto Keccak-256, byte-for-byte; and (3) a full ROUND-TRIP — our GREEN prehashed signer signs a typed Permit digest
# with a TEST key across six deterministic keys, the correct v recovers, recover_typed_signer returns exactly that key's own Ethereum address, and a
# one-byte digest tamper never recovers the true signer. Edge refusals: BadSignatureLength, BadWordLength, BadRecoveryByte, BadAddressLength,
# TypeStringTooLong. Purely local — no key, no network, no funds, no real device.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/cr/crypto_eip712_witness.rish

say "crypto-eip712: Language EN — EIP-712 is the digest a wallet shows a human before it signs \"typed data\": every EIP-2612 permit, every DeFi order, every gasless meta-transaction, every typed Sign-in-with-Ethereum. Where EIP-191 personal_sign frames a flat string, EIP-712 hashes a TREE of typed fields against a domain separator, so a signature for one contract on one chain can never be replayed against another. This module composes three already-GREEN rungs and authors none of its own cryptography."
say "crypto-eip712: Style Radiant — the law is stated positively: type_hash hashes the canonical type string; word_from_address and word_from_u64 encode atomic fields; encode_string hashes a dynamic field; hash_struct concatenates keccak256(type_hash ‖ fields); eip712_domain_separator binds a signature to one app on one chain at one contract; eip712_digest frames keccak256(0x19 0x01 ‖ domain_separator ‖ struct_hash); recover_typed_signer reads the signer back out — so the same typed message and signature always name the same signer, and a tampered field names a different one or none."
say "crypto-eip712: Lens TAME — no new cryptography: every hash is the GREEN crypto/keccak256.rye, every recovery the GREEN crypto/secp256k1_ecrecover.rye, every address the GREEN crypto/eth_address.rye. Fixed shapes (word 32, address 20, digest 32, signature 65), named caps (type string, struct fields), contract asserts on every function, the recovery byte checked before recovery. Parity holds three ways: a PUBLISHED known-answer (the spec's own Ether Mail signature recovers Cow's own published wallet), an INDEPENDENT Zig-Keccak construction byte-for-byte, and a full sign->recover->address round-trip through the GREEN prehashed signer with a one-byte tamper refused. In recovery every value is PUBLIC — no secret leaks; signing with a real identity key stays the custody gate (#3/#4). Purely local — no key, no network, no funds, no device."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "crypto/bin/eip712"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p crypto/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build crypto/eip712.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "crypto-eip712: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "crypto/bin/eip712.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "crypto-eip712: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "crypto-eip712: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN crypto-eip712' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "crypto-eip712: selftest did not print the GREEN crypto-eip712 line"
